    people hunting for a sign-in failure they didn't recognize.

  [1mFirst question: what should people be able to filter by?[0m

  The choice is how many ways to narrow the list. Each extra way adds markup and states that reviewers will check line
  by line, and adds to the ~300-line diff budget.

  - [1mEvent type only.[0m One Select with "All events" plus the nine fixed types (the guideline says one of six or more
    options is a Select). It's the smallest diff and covers the failed-sign-in case directly. Adding more filters later
    is easy.
  - [1mEvent type + date range.[0m It helps people match an event to a day they remember. But the 03 Forms rule for a date
    range is two date pickers plus a presets Select, and dates bring in time zones (the "When" column has to say which
    zone it's in), which is currently a follow-up item. This roughly triples the UI to review.
  - [1mEvent type + text search[0m over device and location. "Firefox on Windows" or "Madrid" would find things the type
    filter can't. That's a Search TextInput with a clear button. It's cheap, but locations are approximate, so a search
    hit could look more exact than it is.

  [1mMy recommendation: event type only.[0m It solves the problem behind the only real tickets, keeps the diff small and the
  review short, and doesn't block adding either of the others.

